/// Synopsis: `#callout`: five kinds in the style `"bar"` (the sixth, `#examples`, on its own page), the function of each kind (`#caution`, `#tip`, `#remark`, `#note`, `#example`) with options, the same text on the line of the label and on the next one (the same space after the label), an icon given as content (in the color of the callout, white on the badge), the style `"badge"`, `title:`, `color:`, `icon:` and `icon: none`, lists, arrows and a code block inside, `#examples`, the example with the title in the plural, in both styles and with `title:`, a callout of two lines in a layout centered vertically and horizontally, in both styles (the icon on the first line, the text on the left), and a text that opens with a shorthand (`->`, `>`, a quote, a `>` alone on the line before an equation), which goes to the line under the title, while an escaped `\>` or a quote followed by text stays on the line of the title. A `-`, `+` or `->` list at the start of a callout goes on the line under the title, with the same room (last page).
#import "../../common.typ": *
#show: setup
#include "body.typ"
